

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 7

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU





          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  German philosopher George Hegel, 1821:
  "In England even the poorest of people believe they have Rights; this is 
very different from what satisfies the poor in other lands."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  The Buccaneer Sea was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in 
the Buccaneer Sea.
  Frigid winter gave way to fragrant spring.  Uga-Buga Makumb's attempted 
cast of the Charm spell was unsuccessful.

  A fleet coming from the empire of Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3) entered Kabompo, 
hoping to subjugate that province ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll and made up of great Seas.  Samantha 
(#95)'s naval forces took control of Kabompo practically uncontested.  
Samantha leads approximately 1 Fleet.
  In early summer, Uga-Buga Makumb practiced his Necromancy and his skill in 
Necromancy went up.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached skill level 7 in Necromancy.  
Your characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "WITCHSIGHT" TALENT: This special Necromancy Talent constantly 
operates by itself, without having to cast a spell.  Whenever an opponent 
turns Invisible in combat, the Necromancer can still see his opponent and is 
unaffected by the spell.


  Ships bearing the battle-standards of the Mbaba (#3)ian empire cruised 
into the Sea province of the Amazonian Sea, a land defended by the forces of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  Samantha (#95)'s naval forces took 
control of the Amazonian Sea practically uncontested.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Uga-Buga Makumb tried to 
improve his Necromancy, but the task was beyond his ability.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Uga-Buga Makumb's 
Skeletal Army spell backfired and Uga-Buga Makumb wound up covered with 
psycho-kinetic goo.
  With the advent of the early winter season Uga-Buga Makumb cast a Skeletal 
Army spell and the 53rd Skeletal Phalanx, the 70th Skeletal Chariots, the 
83rd Skeletal Camel Corps, the 155th Skeletal Chariots and the 267th 
Skeletal Chariots arose from the graves of the dead!

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll for this 
year.


  Uga-Buga Makumb treated with his ally Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Everard (#16) grew bored with the scenery in Jerbilia and left for Tabora.
  Drago (#39) left Chaco to attend a reunion of his old regiment in Big Sky.
  Raiden (#96) heard stories of excellent fishing in the Fourth Sea and left 
the Moonshine Sea to take a vacation there.
  The 42nd Axemen grew tired of the whores of Chaco and moved on off to 
Katanga where they hoped the pickings would be more to their liking.
  The 131st Trolls dissolved their company and went home.

  Sherwood was plundered by the Centaur, who came from out of the dark 
wilderness and pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Uga-Buga Makumb's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 172 gold in revenue.  46 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 102nd Eagles, the 133rd Garrison, the 155th Skeletal Chariots, 
the 166th Garrison, the 198th Trolls and the 206th Dragons trained well and 
improved in quality.  125 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  
Uga-Buga Makumb was left with 93 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Guerin
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring, and I prepared to carry out my imperial 
assignments.  I cast a Kill Enemy spell and Alaric was magically killed by a 
dark Necromantic spell!  Thus did Alaric die, a defiant death by any 
standard.  His possessions were burned with Alaric on the funeral pyre.
  During early summer, Alaric was resurrected by the spell cast by me.
  With the coming of the late summer season I marched on Peachwood (#1202) 
with my formidable forces.  Northeast of here is Gnarlia (#1301), a Forest 
province owned by Kahn, where Humans dwell.  Their Human fighters array 
themselves in the style of Bowmen and Light Cavalry.  To the northwest there 
is a Jungle province known as Dirkwood (#1201), a land of Dragons where 
no one reigns.  If need be, they can muster a host of Dragons to defend 
their territory.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll ordered an invasion force into the 
Forest province of Peachwood, owned by the provincial Ent chieftain.  I 
commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the 
provincial Ent chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Peachwood (1202):

