  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 109th Heavy Cavalry and the 277th Eagles in reserve. 
Standing tall with my warriors was I.  No generals were present to lead the 
forces of the provincial Ent chieftain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The luck of Guerin's men was running high on this 
occasion, for my men were in good spirits from a recent successful 
plundering expedition, and I thus enjoyed a significant edge.  Also, I 
maneuvered my troops against the provincial Ent chieftain with great 
tactical foresight and obtained a tremendous tactical superiority.

  On the left flank, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 129th Ents.  
The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 129th Ents and attacked 
without mercy.  The 110th Bowmen flanked the enemy and charged in with full 
strength.
  I maneuvered the 124th Skeletal Dragons to the front line, as a strategem 
for a superior match-up.  The terrified soldiers of the 129th Ents were 
hideously scorched by the fire-spitting Dragons.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons 
battled with the 129th Ents and smashed their heads as if they were 
eggplants.
  On the right outside wing, the Crack 240th Bowmen were inspired to 
fanatiscm by me, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced the 
128th Ents.  The 241st Bowmen flanked the enemy lines and attacked with full 
force.  The 277th Eagles swooped down on the 128th Ents and attacked them.  
The 240th Bowmen battled the 128th Ents and mowed them down like weeds.
  The host of Guerin finally crushed the army of the provincial Ent 
chieftain's morale with one last, great push.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons 
annihilated the 129th Ents.  The 240th Bowmen slew the 128th Ents almost to 
a man.
  Guerin's campaign accomplished the conquest of Peachwood.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the 124th Skeletal Dragons was greatly 
buoyed by the exciting battle.  We now rate it a proud Veteran unit.  The 
240th Bowmen was tested during the battle and came through with flying 
colors.  We can now call it an Elite unit.  We could not have been better 
satisfied with the fighting spirit of the 110th Bowmen, and we have raised 
its rating to Crack.  Guerin's efforts improved my skill in Tactics.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I cast a Plague spell.  
Sherwood was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 143rd Light Cavalry in 
Sherwood and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 144th Legion in Sherwood 
and destroyed them.  The plague struck the 214th Fleet in Sherwood and 
destroyed them.  The plague struck the 219th Legion in Sherwood and 
destroyed them.  The plague struck the 221st Light Cavalry in Sherwood and 
destroyed them.
  With the coming of the early winter season I marched on Sherwood (#1302) 
with my command.  Turning to the northeast, one espies a Sea area, which is 
known as San Andreas (#1401).  It is populated by no races and no one rules 
there.  East of here is Damnonia (#1402), a poor Plain province owned by 
Kahn, where Humans dwell.  Their Human fighters fight as Legion.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at Sherwood, a Forest province owing allegiance to Kahn 
(#6).  I commanded the attacking armies.  The defending forces were 
commanded by Kahn.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown 
here:

