  DEFENDING ARMY

  I led my armies into the fray.  Standing tall with his warriors was Kahn.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The army of Kahn used magic to aid their cause.  Magical 
phantasmal armies fought with hiss soldiers.  Guerin's luck seemed to be 
running low, as the engagement's unexpected field of battle caught my 
soldiers somewhat unprepared.  Kahn's men thus gained a significant edge.  
On the other hand I maneuvered my forces against Kahn with excellent 
tactical foresight and consequently enjoyed a tremendous tactical advantage.
  Kahn's troops were prepared to struggle like tigers for their fatherland.
  Out on the left outside flank, the Elite 240th Bowmen were encouraged to 
berserk fanatiscm by me, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced 
the 218th Legion, who were blessed by a retinue of priests sent by the 
League of Pagan Clerics, which inspired them to a fanatical fury.  In this 
sector, the 240th Bowmen were slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of 
ground and they joined the fight at a tiny disadvantage.  The 240th Bowmen 
fought the 218th Legion and fought them tooth and nail, neither side willing 
to give ground.
  Within the interior lines, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 184th 
Bowmen.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 188th Bowmen and 
attacked them.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons were decimated by the arrows 
fired by the pesky Bowmen.  The 277th Eagles soared over the 184th Bowmen 
and attacked without mercy.  The 277th Eagles were bothered by the fire of 
their feared Bowmen enemy.  On this field, some men of the 184th Bowmen had 
been drawn away by spurious rumors of a raid elsewhere, and joined the 
battle at a hefty disadvantage.  It appeared that the 108th Skeletal Bowmen 
would win the battle.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The regimental band of the 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen was squashed by a boulder hurled from a catapult, which 
greatly deflated the spirits of the troops.  Still, the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen fought with the 184th Bowmen and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the right wing, the Crack 110th Bowmen were encouraged to selfless 
fanatiscm by me, their revered First Elder of Elvenkind.  They were arrayed 
against the Crack 142nd Legion.  Here, the 142nd Legion were held off by the 
earthen ramparts built up by their opponents.  The 142nd Legion expended a 
great many soldiers in fighting over it.  The 110th Bowmen battled with the 
142nd Legion and fought them to a standstill.
  Guerin's armies vanquished the army opposing them with a final charge.  
The 108th Skeletal Bowmen destroyed the 184th Bowmen.  The 124th Skeletal 
Dragons overtook the enemy in their headlong retreat and slew the 142nd 
Legion almost to a man.  The 277th Eagles chased after the enemy and were 
beaten off by the 218th Legion in a tough rearguard action.
  Sherwood was overrun by the forces of Guerin.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the 277th Eagles fought determinedly during the 
battle and came through with a good effort.  We can now call it a Veteran 
unit.  Kahn retreated to Quantara Roo with what remained of his forces.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into spring.  I failed in my ineffectual attempt to 
cast a Skeletal Army spell.

  In Limerick, Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll brought to bay 
Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3).  I commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders 
were commanded by Mbaba.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Limerick (0703):

                                326th             
                               Dragons            
                               01           
                                                  
