  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing tall with my warriors was I.  Lady of Beer Mbaba stood 
determinedly at the head of her thousands.
  I stepped forward and challenged Mbaba to personal combat.  
Lady of Beer Mbaba answered the challenge to honorable combat.  I chanted my 
mysterious words of magic and cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Mbaba quake 
and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  Mbaba loped along steadily and closed to bow range.  Chanting my words of 
magic with trained precision, I let fly a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist 
in the shape of a cross formed around me.  My experience raised my skill in 
White Magic.
  Congratulations!  You have attained level 5 in White Magic.  At levels 5 
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped at 3 Action, 2
Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" spells are also 
capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine who attacks 
first in personal combat).  Instead, your characters of this high level gain 
the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  Mbaba closed to melee range, filled with uncontrolled blood-lust.  Mbaba 
swang at me but I evaded the sword.  I attempted to help my cause with a 
Hand Of Death spell, but it sputtered at the last second.  Mbaba thrust at 
her nemesis but her aim was just off the mark.  I turned away Mbaba with my 
spirited assault.  I then swang at Mbaba with maximum force and missed by a 
mile.
  Mbaba treacherously thrust at me but her sword whiffed through the air.  I 
daringly swang at Mbaba and inflicted 5 damage points.  Mbaba maneuvered for 
a better attacking vantage.  Then Mbaba swang at me with all her might and 
scored 1 damage points on me.  I flamboyantly vaulted over Mbaba and 
contemptuously swang at her and would have struck her if Mbaba hadn't 
sidestepped.
  Showing no fear, Mbaba swang at me but I evaded the blow.  I swang at 
Mbaba but my aim was just off.  Mbaba faked one way, then switched over and 
swang at me and scored on me, doing 1 points of damage.  I violently 
assailed Mbaba and damaged her, scoring 4 damage points.
  With amazing speed, Mbaba thrust at me and walloped me with 1 damage 
points.  I summoned all my strength and bravely swang at my nemesis and 
inflicted 5 damage points.  Mbaba was fatally wounded.  And so it was that 
Mbaba met her tragic end.
  The forces commanded by Lady of Beer Mbaba were disheartened by her 
demise, but still they moved forward with some hope of victory.  As luck 
would have it, Teleko's formations were well hidden by a sudden mist, giving 
them a small edge.  Also, tactical supremacy was guaranteed by Teleko's 
powerful tactical genius.
  The Dragons commanded by me were not impressed by my strange appearance.  
The Orcs commanded by Mbaba were disgusted with her strange appearance.
  Out on the left flank, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 67th Legion and 
drove them back with a savage fury.
  Within the interior front, the Veteran 320th Eagles were arrayed against 
the 15th Phalanx.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 15th Phalanx and 
attacked them.  The 320th Eagles battled the 15th Phalanx and smashed their 
heads as if they were eggplants.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the Crack 234th Legion.  
The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 234th Legion and attacked without 
mercy.  On this field, an officer of the 322nd Eagles noticed an opening in 
the enemy lines which had opened when they skirted a wide rock formation.  
Charging into the gap, the 322nd Eagles gained a considerable advantage.  
The 322nd Eagles battled the 234th Legion and gradually pushed them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 319th Eagles were arrayed against the 
235th Legion.  The 319th Eagles soared over the 235th Legion and attacked 
them.  The 326th Dragons swooped down on the 235th Legion and attacked them. 
The 319th Eagles battled with the 235th Legion and cut them down like 
beanstalks.
  On the right outside flank, the 321st Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 
321st Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked them.  The 321st 
Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and squashed them like rotten oranges.
  Having found a vulnerable spot in the line of the host of Mbaba, a final 
savage slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the day for me.  The 
323rd Trolls annihilated the 67th Legion.  The 320th Eagles destroyed the 
15th Phalanx.  The 322nd Eagles scattered the 234th Legion in all 
directions.  The 319th Eagles slew the 235th Legion almost to a man.  The 
321st Eagles demolished the 261st Phalanx.
  Teleko's well-planned campaign accomplished the conquest of Limerick.  The 
battle affected the quality of our forces:  the 320th Eagles was tested 
during the battle and came through with a good effort.  We can now rank it a 
Crack unit.  The 322nd Eagles was greatly buoyed by the exciting battle.  We 
now designate it a Veteran unit.  The 321st Eagles proved its valor during 
the fight and we now rate it a Veteran unit.  Its forces completely 
destroyed, the acting commander escaped alone to the Daedalus Sea.
  Windy spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Teleko's Skeletal 
Army spell fizzled and I wound up with my face covered with psycho-kinetic 
slime.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I cast a spell giving magical 
powers of oratory to me.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I flew over to 
the Daedalus Sea.  To the northeast there lies a Plain province known as 
Kilkenny (#801), a land of Humans where Hokuto rules.  Their Human fighters 
array themselves as Legion.  Northwest of here is Starhaven (#701), a rich 
Forest area ruled by Hokuto, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors 
traditionally array themselves in the style of Legion and Chariots.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
entered the Daedalus Sea, hoping to conquer that province owned by 
Lady of Beer Mbaba and made up of great Plains.  Teleko's forces encountered 
little resistance in the Daedalus Sea and I there established our rule.  The 
Daedalus Sea was found to have a tax base of 5 gold.
  During early winter, I rode my flying armies over to Berga.  Northwest of 
here is Cretacia (#601), a rich Mountain province ruled by Hokuto, where 
Dwarves dwell.  Their Dwarven warriors prefer to array themselves as Axemen 
and Light Cavalry.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Berga, a Desert 
area ruled by Lady of Beer Mbaba.  Teleko's forces encountered little 
resistance in Berga and I there established our rule.  Berga was discovered 
to have an income of 1 gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into fragrant spring.  Melantheus invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early summer season Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task was beyond his natural aptitude.  In his sagely 
researches, he discovered a fabulous invention called the Pony Express!  The 
following benefits are conferred by the Pony Express:
  The Pony Express enables the Kingdom to establish fast, consistent lines 
of communication between troops and characters, enabling faster movement of 
armies.  Its effect is to raise the March ability of all of the characters 
of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  In late summer, in his sagely researches, Melantheus discovered a fabulous 
invention called the Meditation Incense!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Meditation Incense:
  Meditation Incense is a fragrant, calming incense which allows the user to 
attain a state of mind that is closer to Nature.  Its effect is to raise the 
Druid ability of all of the characters of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in Druidism.  Your characters 
of this exalted level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  DRUIDIC HORSE CONTROL:  The Druid is able to calm horses who are 
threatened in battle by the various beasts that frighten them.  As a result, 
cavalry units directly led by the Druid no longer have the "Beasts" nemesis 
listed in the Army Type Table.

  In fall, Melantheus was instructed in Sageness by Amalric.  Melantheus 
practiced enthusiastically and improved his skill in Sageness.
  At levels 5 and up, there is not necessarily an increase in the chance to 
invent something.  Instead, the Sage attracts a company of philosphers and 
builds a University in his province of birth.  All characters of this 
exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  In his sagely researches, Melantheus discovered a fabulous invention 
called the Hand-Held Radar!  The following benefits are conferred by the 
Hand-Held Radar:
  Hand-Held Radar sets are distributed to all characters employed by the 
Kingdom.  They enable characters to find features regardless of whether a 
Hide Feature spell has been cast on the feature by an Illusionist.

  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Melantheus practiced his 
Sageness and improved noticeably.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 6 in Sageness.  
Your characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Melantheus discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.
  Melantheus heard a rumor telling of a feature in Tabora (#705), a Desert 
Ruins where dwells the Beholder.  The Desert Ruins is reputed to contain the 
Large Hoard of Gold.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


