  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 77th Fleet Marines, the 97th Garrison and the 298th 
Garrison in reserve.  I led my armies into the battle.  Standing at the 
ready with his warriors was Kurtinaitis.
  No luck of noteworthy importance affected the engagement.  In this 
perilous slugging match, I seemed to gain the tactical upper hand.

  Across the whole front, the 78th Bowmen were arrayed against the 162nd 
Bowmen.  The 297th Axemen and the 296th Fleet Marines flanked the enemy and 
charged in with full strength.  On this field, the 162nd Bowmen were 
slightly disrupted by a slippery patch of ground and they joined battle at a 
tiny disadvantage.  The 78th Bowmen fought the 162nd Bowmen and gradually 
pushed them back.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Kurtinaitis, a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the battle for me.  
The 296th Fleet Marines gave chase and were beaten off by the 162nd Bowmen 
in a tough rearguard battle.
  Though Tao-Li's forces were victorious, Kurtinaitis rallied his men and 
prepared to contest the Plesiosaurus Sea.  The battle affected the quality 
of our forces:  the mayhem wreaked by the 78th Bowmen in the battle has 
elevated the spirits of its warriors, and all agree that it has achieved 
Veteran status.
  With the advent of the early summer season I could not hire Kurtinaitis 
because Kurtinaitis rules his own province.  So, I tried to improve my 
Tactics, but the task was beyond my aptitude.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  I attempted an illegal 
move.  I could not move to Oceanus Cyclopia because armies can't move 
overland and use transport in the same turn.  Instead, I tried to improve my 
Tactics, but the task seemed beyond my natural aptitude.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I tried to move from the 
Plesiosaurus Sea to Mammoth, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal!  
Instead, I practiced my Tactics for months, but could make no significant 
headway.
  With the coming of the early winter season I tried to move from the 
Plesiosaurus Sea to Quantara Roo, a non-adjacent province.  This is illegal! 
So, I practiced my Tactics well but could not improve my skill in Tactics.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
aptitude.  I invented nothing worthy of note in my sagely researches.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  I tried to practice my Sageness,
but the task seemed beyond my natural aptitude.  I invented nothing valuable 
in my sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I tried to 
improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my aptitude.  I invented 
nothing worthy of note in my sagely experiments.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I was instructed in 
Sageness by Magnus.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond 
my aptitude.  My efforts raised my aptitude in Sageness.  I invented nothing 
in my sagely researches.
  Speaking to some friendly farmers, I heard a rumor about a Glade in the 
Near-Beer Sea (#907), occupied by the Centaur.  They say that the Centaur 
owns the Huge Hoard of Gold.
  The fall season cooled into the stillness of early winter.  I was tutored 
in the art of Sageness by Amalric.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the 
task was beyond my natural ability.  My efforts raised my aptitude in 
Sageness.  I discovered nothing in my sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring, and Amalric made ready to carry out his 
imperial assignments.  In his sagely researches, he discovered a fabulous 
invention called the Ultraviolet Lenses!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Ultraviolet Lenses:
  Ultraviolet Lenses are given to all characters employed by the Kingdom to 
enable them to see through an Illusory Terrain spell cast by an Illusionist.

  In early summer, Amalric invented nothing in his sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer came.  Amalric invented 
nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.
  While carousing with fellow adventurers in a tavern, Amalric heard mention 
of a feature in Sherwood (#1302): a Hollow Tree occupied by the Centaur, who 
holds the Projector of Scenic Illusions.
  With the advent of the fall season Amalric was instructed in Sageness by 
Magnus.  Amalric studied and practiced his Sageness and his skill in 
Sageness went up.
  All characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Amalric discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely experiments.
  Speaking with friendly adventurers, Amalric heard a rumor about a 
previously unknown Altar in Tabora (#705), held by the Giant Eagle, who 
according to legend possesses the Large Hoard of Gold.
  With the advent of the early winter season, Amalric discovered nothing 
valuable in his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Amalric


From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I announced a call for volunteers in Mare Tarkium and was able 
to form the 206th Dragons to fight for me.
  Windy spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  I flew over to 
Falkenheim.
  With the coming of the late summer season I levied the 102nd Eagles in 
Falkenheim to serve me.
  In fall, I flew over to Kumasi.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll sent an invasion force into the Jungle 
province of Kumasi, owned by the provincial Troll chieftain.  I was in 
command of the attacking armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the 
provincial Troll chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kumasi (1205):

  123rd   
  Eagles  
    01    
          
  334th   
  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
          
 333rd/V  
  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
----------
    GC    
 131st/A  
  Trolls  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 102nd Eagles, the 206th Dragons and the 249th 
Dragons in reserve.  Standing tall with my warriors was I.  No generals were 
present to lead the forces of the provincial Troll chieftain.
  A bad omen manifested itself, which dealt a telling blow to Odysseus's 
hopes.  It seems that Odysseus's mount was shot down while I was giving a 
speech.  As the battle intensified, the tactical abilities of the provincial 
Troll chieftain and I seemed well matched.
  I was frustrated by the Dragons, who virtually ignored my commands.  The 
Eagles led by me were disgusted with my strange appearance.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 333rd Bowmen were arrayed against the 
131st Trolls.  The 334th Bowmen flanked the undermanned enemy and attacked 
with full force.  The 123rd Eagles soared over the 131st Trolls and attacked 
them.  Here, the commander of the 333rd Bowmen engaged his opposite number 
in single combat.  He unhorsed him and buried his sword in his brain, and 
the 333rd Bowmen jubilantly charged ahead.  The 333rd Bowmen battled with 
the 131st Trolls and gradually shoved them back.
  Odysseus's armies vanquished the army opposing them with a final 
determined charge.  The 334th Bowmen overtook the enemy in their headlong 
retreat and scattered the 131st Trolls in all directions.
  Odysseus's host ended the campaign victoriously and conquered the province 
of Kumasi.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we can raise the 
rating of the 334th Bowmen to Veteran, its officers having displayed 
admirable courage.  After the battle was over, the dismembered trolls 
reformed into a disgruntled band of mercenaries.
  During early winter, I recruited enough men in Kumasi to create the 198th 
Trolls for the army of Odysseus.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I travelled to the Mermaid Sea.  While adventuring, I saw no 
monster.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I rode into the Buccaneer 
Sea.  In my travels, I saw no monsters.
  In late summer, I spoke urgently to Marlboro of the greatness of Uga-Buga 
Makumb's empire and convinced Marlboro to pledge his allegiance to Uga-Buga 
Makumb.  After talking to Marlboro, I judged him (a Human well known for 
Tactics) to have an Evil, Brave nature.
  With the advent of the fall season I moved into the Moonshine Sea.  I 
encountered no monster.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I journeyed to Tabora.  I 
encountered no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Elmer


From: Presto
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I unsheathed my weapon and entered the Cave cautiously.  I 
encountered the Medusa.  Gesturing with my arms, I orchestrated supernatural 
forces of magic, casting an Invisibility spell, fading into invisibility.  I 
searched soundlessly for its treasure.  My greedy fingers twitched in 
anticipation when I saw the vault.  I succeeded in laying my greedy fingers 
on the valuable treasure.  I grabbed the Large Hoard of Gold, my eyes 
glittering with greed.  I pilfered 16 gold from its treasure chest.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Cave.  I encountered no 
monsters.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I travelled to the Dolphin Sea.
In my travels, I saw no monster.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  I approached the 
Hollow Tree, meaning to uncover its mysteries.  I encountered 
the Renegade Swordsman.  I incanted the magic words for an Invisibility 
spell, but bit my tongue and botched the spell.  I searched soundlessly for 
his treasure.  My greedy fingers twitched in anticipation when I saw the 
vault.  I then beheld the treasure, which lay there just for the taking.  
Like walking on a razor's edge, I slowly curled my fingers around the Large 
Hoard of Gold.  I stole 23 gold from the Renegade Swordsman.  Presto's 
experience raised my skill in Thievery.  I hailed the Magic Circle.
  Magic runes formed on the Magic Circle, saying "The Magic Circle will try 
to increase your skill in Illusions by 1 point per visit, up to a maximum of 
4.  If you have low aptitude, your chance of success is halved for every 
aptitude-level you are deficient in Illusions.  You must pay 10 gold each 
time the Magic Circle is used (to show that you accept these terms, a 
character must give two Scout orders when he Searches this feature.)"  I 
encountered no monsters.
  In fall, I gathered my courage and nervously entered the Altar.  I 
encountered the Renegade Necromancer.  Raising my hands high in the air, I 
cast an Invisibility spell, fading into invisibility.  I stole towards 
the Renegade Necromancer's treasure, visions of wealth dancing before my 
eyes.  Despite my caution, I was perceived by the Renegade Necromancer 
before anything could be taken and engaged at melee range.  
The Renegade Necromancer attacked me but her aim was just off the mark.  I 
ran shamelessly and fled from the encounter.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Altar.  During my travels, I 
was confronted by a Minotaur.  Deciding that discretion is sometimes the 
better part of valor, I fled unceremoniously from the dangerous combat.

  During early winter, I rode into Falkenheim.  While adventuring, I 
encountered no monsters.

  Thy humble servant,   Presto


From: Tattoo, Squire to Magnus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  Magnus was tutored in the art of Sageness by 
Lallipugh.  Magnus practiced for many weeks and his skill in Sageness 
increased.  In his sagely researches, he discovered a fabulous invention 
called the Cotton Gin!  The following benefits are conferred by the Cotton 
Gin:
  The Cotton Gin automates the separation of cotton from the seeds contained 
within the cotton bolls, thus freeing all your contented little slaves for 
other productive work.  It has the effect of raising the revenue of the 
Kingdom by an average of 4% each gameturn.

  With the coming of the early summer season, Magnus invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.
  In late summer, Magnus practiced well and improved his ability in Sageness.
  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in Sageness.  At levels 5 and 
up, there is not necessarily an increase in the chance to invent something.  
Instead, the Sage attracts a company of philosphers and builds a University 
in his province of birth.  Your characters of this exalted level are awarded 
the following Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  In his sagely researches, Magnus discovered a fabulous invention called 
the Mithril Chainmail!  The following benefits are conferred by the Mithril 
Chainmail:
  Mithril Chainmail is a specially strengthed armor which enables the wearer 
to swing and maneuver with greater agility in combat.  Its effect is to 
raise the Melee ability of all of the characters of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  With the advent of the fall season, Magnus tried to improve his Sageness, 
but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He discovered nothing valuable in 
his sagely experiments.
  The fall season cooled into the stillness of early winter.  Magnus was 
tutored in Sageness by Melantheus.  Magnus tried to practice his Sageness, 
but the task was beyond his natural aptitude.  His efforts raised his 
aptitude in Sageness.  He discovered nothing in his sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Magnus


From: Gridley, Squire to Clarambald
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring, and Clarambald made ready to carry out 
her urgent orders.  She spoke eloquently to Kari and convinced her to pledge 
her allegiance to Uga-Buga Makumb.  After talking to Kari, Clarambald judged 
her (a Dwarf famous for Marches) to have an Evil, Berserk character.
  With the coming of the early summer season, Clarambald cast a Flood spell 
and Ngara was magically flooded.
  In late summer, Clarambald approached the Dungeon with every intention of 
prevailing over it and whatever guardian beast lay within it.  Clarambald 
encountered the Chimera.  Lifting her hands high in the air, Clarambald cast 
a Fireball spell and walloped the Chimera with 7 damage points.
  The Chimera menacingly advanced to bow range.  Gesturing with her arms, 
Clarambald orchestrated supernatural forces of magic, casting an Ice 
Suspension spell, and a shell of frigid ice formed around the Chimera.  
The Chimera dropped, suffering 9 damage points.  Clarambald's experience 
improved her skill in Element Magic.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in Element Magic.
At levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Element Magic is 
capped at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Tornadoes", "Fireball" 
and "Ice Suspension" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level 
will still determine who attacks first in personal combat).   Instead, your 
characters of this exalted level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The Elemental Mage is now able to use 
the magic of certain Elemental Places of Power to increase the success 
chance of spells.  At any Sacred Rock, Mountain Peak or Ancient Megaliths, 
the success chance to cast an Elemental Magic spell is increased by 20%.  
For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied when that type of feature is 
searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is applied if that feature type is 
in the same province as the character, and is not occupied by a monster.
  In its stunned state, the Chimera could not decide what to do about its 
predicament.
  Clarambald boldly fired an arrow at the Chimera and inflicted 1 damage 
points.  The Chimera dropped to the ground, mortally pierced.  Clarambald 
turned her attention to the hoard of the Chimera.  Clarambald secured the 
Book of Druidic Incantations.  Clarambald examined the Book of Druidic 
Incantations and discovered the following properties:
  The Book of Druidic Incantations raises your Druidic ability by one level. 
For example, a skill level of 0 would rise to skill level 1.  The reader of 
this strangely compelling work becomes completely engrossed with it, and 
after this book is perused, it crumbles to dust and merges with the sands of 
time.  Use the "Use Item" Action to invoke its powers.
  Clarambald took 6 gold from the treasure trove of the Chimera.
  While scouting the Dungeon, Clarambald saw a Pool which seemed to be of a 
magical nature.
  Magic runes formed on the Pool, saying "The Pool changes your sex from 
male to female (or vice versa.)  By the power of the Pool, I change you to a 
woman!  Hee hee, how does your armor fit you NOW!"  Clarambald encountered 
no monsters.
  During fall, Clarambald's attempted cast of the Flood spell didn't work.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  Clarambald moved into Limerick. 
She saw no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Clarambald


From: Constantine
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I tried to explore Chaco but it seemed that it had already been 
completely explored.  I discovered also that Chaco has been the site of 
terrible battles.  Many intrepid soldiers have perished on its fields: the 
53rd Skeletal Phalanx (Average Elves), the 70th Skeletal Chariots (Crack 
Humans), the 83rd Skeletal Camel Corps (Veteran Humans), the 155th Skeletal 
Chariots (Green Humans), the 267th Skeletal Chariots (Average Humans), the 
282nd Legion (Veteran Humans), the 283rd Legion (Veteran Humans) and the 
284th Chariots (Average Humans).  My efforts raised my prowess in Exploring. 
I saw no marauding monsters.
  In early summer, I was tutored in Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I 
practiced my Necromancy and my skill in Necromancy went up.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I was tutored in 
the art of Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  I practiced my Necromancy and 
improved substantially.
  With the coming of the fall season I was tutored in the art of Marches by 
Kari.  I practiced enthusiastically and improved my skill in Marches.
  In early winter, I was instructed in the art of Marches by Pascal.  I 
practiced for months and my skill in Marches increased.

  Thy humble servant,   Constantine


From: Montgomery, Squire to Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to sweet spring.  Pascal rode into Chaco.  He marched 
along an unusual route through Chaco and raised our level of exploration 
there to 100%.  Pascal discovered a Tomb (#27) in Chaco, inhabited by 
the Balrog Demon.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  
Conjurers cringe in fear at the very mention of the Balrog Demon, an awful 
winged whirlwind of scorching fire and slashing steel.  It is a highly evil 
and very powerful monster indeed.  In his travels, he saw no monsters.
  During early summer, Pascal was tutored in the art of Necromancy by 
Uga-Buga Makumb.  Pascal studied and practiced his Necromancy and his skill 
in Necromancy went up.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer came.  Pascal was tutored 
in the art of Necromancy by Uga-Buga Makumb.  Pascal rehearsed and practiced 
his Necromancy and improved noticeably.
  With the advent of the fall season Pascal was tutored in Marches by Kari.  
Pascal practiced well and improved his skill in Marches.
  During early winter, Pascal was tutored in the art of Marches by Kari.  
Pascal practiced for many weeks and his skill in Marches increased.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Pascal


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  Alaric recruited 
the 133rd Garrison and the 166th Garrison from among the population of Bir 
Nzaran, to serve under the provincial garrison commander.
  With the advent of the fall season, Alaric travelled to Peachwood.
  During early winter, Alaric journeyed to Sherwood.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alaric


From: Marlboro
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  The summer surrendered to fall.  I moved into the Valiant Sea.  While 
adventuring, I saw no monsters.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I rode into Tebessa.  While 
adventuring, I encountered no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlboro


From: Kari
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  During early summer, I travelled to Ngara.  While adventuring, I 
encountered no monster.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer arrived.  I journeyed to Chaco.  I 
encountered no monster.
  With the coming of the fall season I tried to improve my Marches, but the 
task seemed beyond my ability.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I tried to practice my 
Marches, but the task seemed beyond my ability.

  Thy humble servant,   Kari


STATE OF THE NATION:

  My lord and sovereign, greatest of Kings, I humbly beg thy leave to make
report of matters of this Kingdom that may concern thy divine majesty.


DIPLOMACY 

  My lord, the following Kings have wisely allied with thy ever-
victorious majesty:                    

  Babba Sissoko (#0), 176g taxbase, 84g in treasury is of Undead alignment.
  Agesilao (#9)


  My lord, the following Kings are foolishly at war with thy ever-
victorious majesty:                    

  Mbaba (#3), 12g taxbase, 43g in treasury
  Hokuto (#4), 37g taxbase, 6g in treasury is of Divine alignment.
  Prometeo (#5)
  Kahn (#6), 15g taxbase, 18g in treasury
  Giovanna d'Arco (#7)
  Circe (#8), 16g taxbase, 23g in treasury


  My lord, the following Kings are cautiously neutral with thy ever-
victorious majesty:                    

  Bradipo I (#2)


  Babba Sissoko is King #0, Andrea Ferrigno, ,  ,      , a Orcish , Undead 
ruler, (>InterNet:cbbhaf@tin.it).  
  Mbaba is King #3, Guido Pacifici, ,  ,      , a Human ruler, 
(>InterNet:guidopacifici@hotmail.com).  
  Hokuto is King #4, Mario Pascoli, ,  ,      , a Human , Divine ruler, 
(>InterNet:mario.pascoli@fastwebnet.it).  
  Kahn is King #6, Lorenzo Cammoranesi, ,  ,      , a Human ruler, 
(>InterNet:orione@mclink.it).  
  Circe is King #8, Marco Calabresi, ,  ,      , a Human ruler, 
(>InterNet:brainwave_mc@yahoo.it).  


FINANCES

  O Great One, I submit for thy examination the following figures
concerning the finances of our great nation:                     

  Gold in treasury:   93
  Expected Revenues: 164
   +Invention Bonus:   6%
  Expected Expenses: 171


  Our Kingdom is also benefited by the following Discoveries of the Sages:

  Pony Express             (+1 skill in Marches)
(Sent to player(s) #0 by scientific treaty)    

  Meditation Incense       (+1 skill in Druidism)
  Ultraviolet Lenses       (Anti-spell: Illusory Terrain)
  Dry Ice Fog              (Anti-spell: Clairvoyance)
  Analytical Psychology    (Anti-spell: Charm)
  Cotton Gin               (+4% revenue)
  Postage Stamp            (+2% revenue)
  Strength Elixir          (+1 skill in Meleeing)
  Mithril Chainmail        (+1 skill in Meleeing)
  Hand-Held Radar          (Anti-spell: Hide Feature)


