GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In spring, Mammoth was conquered by Riose (#52)'s host.
  In late summer, Saladin (#14) moved into Mare Tarkium.
  In late summer, Tlazolteotl (#88) flew into Trouthome.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Trouthome, a 
Desert area owned by Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced 
little resistance in Trouthome and Tlazolteotl there established our rule.
  In spring, Bagmore (#75) rode his flying armies into the Albatross Sea.

Kingdom of Mbaba (#3):
  In spring, Lady of Beer Mbaba (#3) stood determinedly at the head of her 
thousands.
  And so it was that Mbaba met her tragic end.  The forces commanded by 
Lady of Beer Mbaba were disheartened by her demise, but still they moved 
forward with some hope of victory.  The Orcs commanded by Mbaba were 
disgusted with her strange appearance.
  Out on the right flank, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 323rd Trolls battled with the 67th Legion and 
drove them back with a savage fury.
  Within the interior front, the Veteran 320th Eagles were arrayed against 
the 15th Phalanx.  The 320th Eagles soared over the 15th Phalanx and 
attacked them.  The 320th Eagles battled the 15th Phalanx and smashed their 
heads as if they were eggplants.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the Crack 234th Legion.  
The 322nd Eagles swooped down on the 234th Legion and attacked without 
mercy.  On this field, an officer of the 322nd Eagles noticed an opening in 
the enemy lines which had opened when they skirted a wide rock formation.  
Charging into the gap, the 322nd Eagles gained a considerable advantage.  
The 322nd Eagles battled the 234th Legion and gradually pushed them back.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 319th Eagles were arrayed against the 
235th Legion.  The 319th Eagles soared over the 235th Legion and attacked 
them.  The 326th Dragons swooped down on the 235th Legion and attacked them. 
The 319th Eagles battled with the 235th Legion and cut them down like 
beanstalks.
  On the left outside flank, the 321st Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 
321st Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked them.  The 321st 
Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and squashed them like rotten oranges.  Its 
forces completely destroyed, the acting commander escaped alone to the 
Daedalus Sea.
  In early winter, Mbaba treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Mbaba (#3) 
treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Mbaba (#3) treated with her ally 
Prometeo (#5).  Mbaba (#3) treated with her ally Kahn (#6).  Mbaba (#3) 
treated with her ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Mbaba (#3) treated with her 
ally Circe (#8).  Mbaba (#3) treated with her ally Agesilao (#9).

Kingdom of Hokuto (#4):
  In spring, Balmwood was magically flooded.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In early summer, Kahn (#6) searched the Hollow Tree with the intention of 
overcoming it and whatever vile guardian beast lay within.  Kahn encountered 
the Centaur.  Kahn attempted to help his fortunes with a Mirror-Image 
Phantasm spell, but it sputtered at the last second.  The Centaur loped 
along smoothly and closed to bow range.  Kahn thought to attempt a Fireball 
spell, but couldn't find a needed material component before Kahn could make 
his spellcast.  The Centaur fired an arrow at Kahn and inflicted 3 damage 
points on Kahn.  The Centaur boldly fired an arrow at Kahn and damaged Kahn, 
inflicting 2 damage points.  Kahn charged into the melee.  The Centaur 
shifted over to a better defensive position.  Then the Centaur kicked at 
Kahn and inflicted 5 damage points.  Kahn staggered, stunned by the deadly 
blow.  And so it came to pass that Kahn met his tragic end.  Kahn was 
succeeded by his next-in-line (who will use his predecessor's name until 
next turn).
  Kahn saw nothing special while scouting out the Hollow Tree.  Sherwood was 
hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 143rd Light Cavalry in Sherwood and 
destroyed them.  The plague struck the 144th Legion in Sherwood and 
destroyed them.  The plague struck the 214th Fleet in Sherwood and destroyed 
them.  The plague struck the 219th Legion in Sherwood and destroyed them.  
The plague struck the 221st Light Cavalry in Sherwood and destroyed them.  
Gladstone cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were formed for 
Kahn.  Standing tall with his warriors was Kahn.
  The army of Kahn used magic to aid their cause.  Magical phantasmal armies 
fought with hiss soldiers.  Kahn's troops were prepared to struggle like 
tigers for their fatherland.
  Out on the right outside flank, the Elite 240th Bowmen faced the 218th 
Legion, who were blessed by a retinue of priests sent by the League of Pagan 
Clerics, which inspired them to a fanatical fury.  In this sector, the 240th 
Bowmen's commander cleverly unleashed a herd of pink-painted elephants to 
make his opponents imagine they were going crazy, but the ruse had little 
effect except to amuse them.  The 240th Bowmen battled the 218th Legion and 
fought them to a standstill.
  In the interior lines, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were arrayed 
against the 184th Bowmen.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 
188th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons were 
decimated by the bolts fired by the dangerous Bowmen.  The 277th Eagles 
swooped down on the 184th Bowmen and attacked without mercy.  The 277th 
Eagles were riddled with fire of their dangerous Bowmen enemy.  On this 
battleground, the commander of the 184th Bowmen was flattened by a boulder 
thrown from a catapult, which greatly deflated the spirits of the troops.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The regimental band of the 108th 
Skeletal Bowmen was squashed by a boulder hurled from a catapult, which 
greatly deflated the spirits of the troops.  Still, the 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen fought with the 184th Bowmen and gradually shoved them back.
  Out on the left wing, the Crack 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
Crack 142nd Legion.  Here, the cowardice of a soldier worked against the 
142nd Legion.  They were thrown into disarray when he panicked and ran, 
shouting "The battle is hopeless!  We're all cooked!"  The 110th Bowmen 
fought with the 142nd Legion and battled them tooth and nail, neither side 
willing to give ground.  Kahn retreated to Quantara Roo with what remained 
of his forces.
  In spring, the waters of Mammoth were magically parted.
  In early summer, Charious (#53) travelled to Sherwood.  During his travels 
this season, a Renegade Priest came at Charious like a bolt from the blue.  
Charious spoke to the Renegade Priest with respectful words, and a fight was 
averted.
  In late summer, Gladstone was resurrected by the spell cast by Charious.
  In early summer, Hawkins (#56) journeyed to Sherwood.  During his travels, 
Hawkins was ambushed, pinned down and severely beaten by angry vigilantes.  
Hawkins finally broke free.  A Royal Ranger caught up with Hawkins.  But 
when Hawkins was taken to the local sheriff, Hawkins showed him the official 
seal of Kahn, and was let go.
  In late summer, Fingol (#27) travelled to Sherwood.
  In fall, Gladstone cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were 
formed for Kahn (#6).

Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In spring, Circe (#8) disbanded the 26th Were-Beasts.  Balmwood was 
magically flooded.
  In late summer, Circe journeyed to Chaco.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Trouthome, a 
Desert area owned by Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced 
little resistance in Trouthome and Tlazolteotl there established our rule.
  In spring, Hope (#94) encountered Behemond (#21).  Chanting her silver 
words of magic into a mighty Hand Of Death spell, Hope gestured with her 
hands and began making squeezing motions with her hands.  Behemond stuck his 
tail between his legs and fled from Hope as fast as his legs could carry 
Behemond!


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached level 5 in White Magic.  At levels 5 
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped at 3 Action, 2
Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" spells are also 
capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine who attacks 
first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Necromancy.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Necromancy is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Skeletal Armies", "Plague" and 
"Hand of Death" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will 
still determine who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all 
characters of this exalted level are awarded the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 6 in Necromancy.  
All characters of this exalted level are awarded the following Advanced 
Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- PLACES OF POWER:  The Necromancer is now able to use the magic 
of certain Dark Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  
At any Tomb, Crypt or Catacombs, the success chance to cast a Necromancy 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 7 in Necromancy.  
All characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "WITCHSIGHT" TALENT: This special Necromancy Talent constantly 
operates by itself, without having to cast a spell.  Whenever an opponent 
turns Invisible in combat, the Necromancer can still see his opponent and is 
unaffected by the spell.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained skill level 5 in Element Magic.
At levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in Element Magic is 
capped at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Tornadoes", "Fireball" 
and "Ice Suspension" spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level 
will still determine who attacks first in personal combat).   Instead, all 
characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  ELEMENTAL MAGIC- PLACES OF POWER:  The Elemental Mage is now able to use 
the magic of certain Elemental Places of Power to increase the success 
chance of spells.  At any Sacred Rock, Mountain Peak or Ancient Megaliths, 
the success chance to cast an Elemental Magic spell is increased by 20%.  
For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied when that type of feature is 
searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is applied if that feature type is 
in the same province as the character, and is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Sageness.  At levels 5 
and up, there is not necessarily an increase in the chance to invent 
something.  Instead, the Sage attracts a company of philosphers and builds a 
University in his province of birth.  Your characters of this exalted level 
gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Sageness.  At levels 5 
